---
title: Weeknight Paella
course: main
cuisine: spanish
servings: 2
time_active: 25
time_total: 60
leftovers: good
tags: [weeknight, one-pot]
pairs: [roasted-asparagus]
source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WfYjmrH9gSw
description: Adam Ragusea's streamlined, small-batch Valencian-style paella with chicken wings and green beans.
---

Toast @saffron{1%pinch} dry in a #paella pan{} or 10-inch skillet over medium heat until fragrant, ~{1%minute}. Crush it into a microwave-safe jug, add @white wine{1%cup} and @water{1%cup}, heat until hot, and let it steep.

Oil the pan with @olive oil{} and heat over medium-high. Season @chicken wings{1/2%lb}(6-8 pieces) generously with @salt and @black pepper{}, then brown on all sides until nearly cooked through, ~{10-12%minutes}.

Meanwhile, mince @garlic{2-3%cloves} and @shallot{1}, dice @sweet pepper{1}(small; or half a bell pepper), and trim and halve a handful of @green beans{4%oz}.

Push the wings to the edge of the pan. Cook the garlic, shallot, and pepper in the middle until soft and lightly golden. Stir in @tomato paste{2%tsp} and cook ~{1%minute}, then add the green beans and cook ~{2%minutes}.

Pour in the saffron liquid and salt it until it tastes slightly saltier than you'd like, since the rice will absorb it. Scatter in @paella rice{1%cup}(or other short-grain rice), spread it evenly, and reduce to a high simmer. Don't stir again. Sprinkle water over any spots that dry out before the rice is tender, ~{18-20%minutes}.

When the rice is nearly done, raise the heat to brown the bottom into a crust. Pull it off the heat when you first smell toasting, ~{1-2%minutes}.

Rest at least ~{15%minutes}. Cut a @lemon{1} into wedges. Serve with a wide spoon, scraping up the crust, and squeeze lemon over at the table.

> Swap the wings for a drained can of lima beans for a vegetarian version, and use smoked or sweet paprika (1 tsp) if you have no saffron. Good additions: butter beans, a rosemary sprig laid on top for the last few minutes, or shrimp and mussels pushed into the rice for the last 5–8 minutes.
